flowchart TB
  accTitle: Capacity feedback constrains production
  accDescr: The producer offers work to a bounded buffer. The consumer removes work from the buffer. When capacity is exhausted, feedback pauses or rejects further offers according to policy. When capacity returns, feedback can allow production to resume. This describes flow control, not durability or guaranteed completion.
  P["Producer"] -->|Offer work| Q["Bounded buffer<br/>0 <= size <= K"]
  Q -->|Take work| C["Consumer"]
  Q -.->|Full: pause or reject| P
  C -.->|Removal frees capacity| Q
  class Q pending;
  class C success;

  classDef control fill:#F5F3FF,stroke:#7C3AED,color:#111827;
  classDef neutral fill:#F3F4F6,stroke:#4B5563,color:#111827;
  classDef success fill:#DCFCE7,stroke:#15803D,color:#111827;
  classDef pending fill:#FFFBEB,stroke:#B45309,color:#111827;
  classDef failure fill:#FEE2E2,stroke:#B91C1C,color:#111827;

